  "reason": "Multiprofile avgpool is the strongest known setting for both PCA RNA (0.591 acc / 0.573 F1) and ResNet50 image (0.328 acc), while transformer aggregation is worse for RNA. The key uncertainty is whether fusing these validated unimodal representations adds value over the RNA-only baseline. config_018 tests simple concat fusion of PCA RNA and ResNet50 image under the same multiprofile avgpool settings, isolating the fusion/multimodal effect without introducing untested encoders. This is the best next use of budget because it directly tests the central multimodal question, exploits the strongest profile/aggregation evidence, and will guide whether to invest in weighted fusion, ViT, or alternative RNA encoders."
